{"type": "survey_submit", "survey_type": "post", "puzzle_idx": null, "answers": {"puzzle_1_rate_again": 4, "puzzle_1_guesses": "never", "puzzle_2_rate_again": 5, "puzzle_2_guesses": "few", "puzzle_3_rate_again": 4, "puzzle_3_guesses": "few", "puzzle_1_rating_reason": "I didn't guess for this puzzle at all and used the hints as a way to figure out a guaranteed correct spot rather than to correct a guess. There weren't a lot of definitive columns or rows to go off of as opposed to the previous trial one.", "puzzle_2_rating_reason": "I had to guess 2 squares since I didn't see a logical way to move forward otherwise, and tried one solution and used the hints to make sure I was guessing correctly.", "puzzle_3_rating_reason": "I didn't exactly run into a situation where I couldn't logically deduce the next step, I just started guessing because I figured I wouldn't need to use all the hints and I got impatient so I just used the hints as a way to eliminate decisions I didn't want to make later.", "strategy": "I tried to figure out if there were any columns or rows where all the black and white spaces added up to 10. Once filling those in, tried to fill in any other deductions, crossed out all the blank spaces for places I knew had the right solution. Then for the rest, I tried to see if there were any overlaps between the leftmost/topmost and rightmost/bottommost solutions, and filled in black for the squares I thought had to be black. After that I repeated the process until I ran out of logical deductions and started guessing with assistance from the hints.", "comments": "Puzzle 3 probably felt less hard than 2 because I'd already had practice from doing the previous puzzles. I think I measure how easy or hard a puzzle is based on how much information is given that guarantees I can fill in something for a square at the start of a puzzle, and how many times I have to guess something and verify the answer via a hint. 2 felt the hardest for me because I had to actually wait for hints to arrive because I ran out of things to fill in for the puzzle that I knew were correct."}, "t": "2026-05-20T20:41:52.030092+00:00"}
